ural complexity).\n- **Tests**: All 5 passing.\n\n**Why this is an improvement despite unchanged mass:**\nThe APP framework says Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) trumps APP metrics. By defining `type Item`, the code now clearly documents the shape of insurable items. Future readers (and the developer working on subsequent tests) immediately understand what data to pass. The removed `as string` cast was a smell — it hinted at a type that was too loose. Now the type tells the truth.\n\n---\n\n### Refactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Added `Item` type, tightened parameter typing, removed `as string` cast (Rule 2 — Reveals Intent improvement)\n**Mass Change**: 12 → 12 (unchanged — type-level improvement with no runtime mass impact)\n**Tests**: All 5 passing"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-24-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 5\nRecent Green phase: Added `potion: 40` to the BASE_PREMIUM lookup table — one-line addition completing all four main item types.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 5\nRecent Green phase: Added `potion: 40` to the BASE_PREMIUM lookup table — one-line addition completing all four main item types.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784950042733},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'll start by reading the current implementation and test files to understand the codebase.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5f136e46e97346eb889a