enai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":4375,"output":248,"cacheRead":35072,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":39695,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950113833,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-1c56c2ca-162a-4f68-ad8e-cfaa6f0eb0f7","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_345426e0e572438590adaf30","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 5: Calculate New APP Mass\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n\n```\nexport function quote(\n  items: Item[],\n  _customerContext: { yearsWithMHPCO: number; contractsSoFar: number }\n): number {\n  const componentTypes = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n  const typeCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  let basePremium = 0;\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    basePremium += BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n    if (componentTypes.has(item.type)) {\n      typeCounts[item.type] = (typeCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    }\n  }\n\n  const BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\n  const BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\n  let blockDiscount = 0;\n  for (const ct of componentTypes) {\n    const count = typeCounts[ct] ?? 0;\n    const blocks = Math.floor(count / BLOCK_SIZE);\n    const basePriceForBlock = BLOCK_SIZE * (BASE_PREMIUM[ct] ?? 0);\n    blockDiscount += blocks * (basePriceForBlock - BLOCK_PRICE);\n  }\n\n  return basePremium - blockDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE;\n}\n```\n\n**Component Count**:\n\n| Category | Items | Count | Mass |\n|----------|-------|-------|------|\n| **Constants** | `\"rune\"`, `\"moonstone\"`, `0` (in `{}`), `0` (in `let basePremium`), `0` (×2 in `??` inside for), `0` (×2 in second for `??`), `1` (in `+ 1`), `3` (BLOCK_SIZE), `60` (BLOCK_PRICE), `0` (seed `??` inside second for) | 12 | 12 |\n| **Bindings** | `items`, `_customerContext`, `componentTypes`, `typeCounts`, `basePremium`, `item`, `BLOCK_SIZE`, `BLOCK_PRICE`, `blockDiscount`, `ct`, `count`, `blocks`, `basePriceForBlock` | 13 | 13 |\n| **Invocations** | `new Set(...)`, `componentTypes.has(...)`, `Math.floor(...)`, `BASE_PREMIUM[item.type]` (index), `BASE_PREMIUM[ct]` (index), `typeCounts[item.type]` (read ×1), `??` (×4), `+=` (addition part ×2), `+`, `-`, `*`, iteration of Set via for-of | ~12 | 24 |\n| **Conditionals** | `if (componentTypes.has(item.type))` | 1 | 4 |\n| **Loops** | `for (const item of items)`, `for (const ct of componentTypes)` | 2 | 10 |\n| **Assignments** | `basePremium += ...`, `typeCounts[...] = ...`, `blockDiscount += ...` | 3 | 18 |\n\n**Total New Mass**: 12 + 13 + 24 + 4 + 10 + 18 = **81**\n\n## Mass Comparison\n\n| Metric | Before | After | Delta |\n|--------|--------|-------|-------|\n| Constants | 13 | 12 | -1 |\n| Bindings | 13 | 13 | 0 |\n| Invocations | 30 | 24 | -6 |\n| Conditionals | 0 | 4 | +4 |\n| Loops | 15 | 10 | -5 |\n| Assignments | 12 | 18 | +6 |\n| **Total** | **83** | **81** | **-2** |\n\nNet mass reduced by 2. The biggest win is collapsing two loops (reduce + for-of) into a single pass, dropping from 3 loops to 2 (mass: 15→10).\n\n## Step 6: Document Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n\n- **Naming**: Renamed `base` → `basePremium` (better reveals intent that it's the total premium sum before discounts)\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Extracted `BLOCK_SIZE` and `BLOCK_PRICE` constants with explanatory names; computed `basePriceForBlock` from `BASE_PREMIUM[ct]` rather than hardcoding `75`, making the block discount formula self-documenting (`blockPriceForBlock - BLOCK_PRICE` instead of `75 - 60`)\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: Merged two separate passes over `items` (type counting + premium summing) into a single `for` loop, eliminating duplicate iteration\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: Derived `basePriceForBlock` from `BASE_PREMIUM[ct]` instead of hardcoding `75`, removing the knowledge duplication between `BASE_PREMIUM[\"rune\"] = 25` and the constant `75` (which was really `3 × 25`)\n- **Mass**: Reduced from 83 to 81 (delta -2)\n- **Rule 4 trade-off**: Added 1 conditional (`if componentTypes.has`) and 1 extra assignment, but the clarity gain and loop reduction justifies the small net cost\n\n**Benefits**:\n1. Single-pass algorithm — no redundant iteration\n2. Block discount formula now derived from `BASE_PREMIUM` — if rune/moonstone premiums ever changed, the block discount would automatically adjust\n3. Constants `BLOCK_SIZE` and `BLOCK_PRICE` self-document the business rules\n4. `basePremium` name clearly reveals intent\n\n---\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring**: Merged two-pass iteration into single pass; renamed `base` → `basePremium`; extracted named constants for block discount logic; derived block base price from `BASE_PREMIUM` instead of hardcoding `75`.\n\n**Mass Change**: 83 → 81 (-2)\n\n**Tests**: All 8 passing ✓"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-24-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 8\nRecent Green phase: Added block discount logic — count component types (rune, moonstone), compute blocks of 3, subtract 15 G (75-60) per block from the summed base. Handles 3-rune block at 60 G.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 8\nRecent Green phase: Added block discount logic — count component types (rune, moonstone), compute blocks of 3, subtract 15 G (75-60) per block from the summed base. Handles 3-rune block at 60 G.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784950117023},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'll start by reading the current implementation and test files to understand the codebase before ref"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ab859b0edfb1401580cabb61","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_dd87ee1fd12045119db0c66e","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":242,"output":103,"cacheRead":6144,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6489,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950117043,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-fae8c9ef-96aa-4304-bcda-36bc1bdff4a7","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ab859b0edfb1401580cabb61","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/**\n * MHPCO Claim Office - quote and claim processing logic.\n */\n\n/** Processing fee applied to every quote (in G). */\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\n/** Base premium amounts per item type (in G). */\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\n/** An insurable item. */\ntype Item = {\n  type: string;\n  material: string;\n  enchantment: number;\n  cursed: boolean;\n};\n\n/**\n * Quote: compute the premium for a list of items for a given customer state.\n * Returns the total premium in G (integer).\n */\nexport function quote(\n  items: Item[],\n  _customerContext: { yearsWithMHPCO: number; contractsSoFar: number }\n): number {\n  // Block pricing: exactly 3 alike components get 60 G instead of 75 G\n  const componentTypes = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\n  const typeCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    typeCounts[item.type] = (typeCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n  }\n  const base = items.reduce((sum, item) => {\n    const individual = BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n    return sum + individual;\n  }, 0);\n  // Apply block discounts: each block of 3 alike components replaces 3×25 = 75 with 60\n  let blockDiscount = 0;\n  for (const ct of componentTypes) {\n    const count = typeCounts[ct] ?? 0;\n    const blocks = Math.floor(count / 3);\n    blockDiscount += blocks * (75 - 60);\n  }\n  return base - blockDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE;\n}\n\n/**\n * Process a claim against an existing policy.\n * Returns { payout: number, remainingCap: number }.\n */\nexport function processClaim(\n  policy: { items: Record<string, unknown>[]; insuranceSum: number },\n  damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[]\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } {\n  throw new Error(\"Not implemented\");\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950118037},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_dd87ee1fd12045119db0c66e","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { quote, processClaim } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office\", () => {\n  // === QUOTE TESTS ===\n\n  // Empty item list\n  it(\"should return premium of 5 G for empty item list (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(5);\n  });\n\n  // Single items - base premiums\n  it(\"should quote 105 G for a plain sword (100 base + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(105);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 65 G for a plain amulet (60 base + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(65);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 85 G for a plain staff (80 base + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"staff\", material: \"wood\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(85);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 45 G for a plain potion (40 base + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"potion\", material: \"glass\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(45);\n  });\n\n  // Components\n  it(\"should quote 30 G for a single rune (25 base + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(30);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 55 G for 2 runes (50 base, no block + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }, { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(55);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 65 G for 3 runes (60 block base + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }, { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }, { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(65);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should quote 105 G for 4 runes (100 base, no block + 5 fee)\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote 180 G for 7 runes (175 base, no block + 5 fee)\");\n\n  // \"Alike\" components - clarifying question test\n  it.todo(\"should quote 80 G for 2 runes + 1 moonstone (75 base, no block: different types + 5 fee)\");\n  it.todo(\"should quote 125 G for 3 runes + 3 moonstones (120 base, two separate blocks + 5 fee)\");\n\n  // Modifier scope on multi-item policies\n  it.todo(\"should quote cursed sword (100 base) + plain amulet (60 base) = 160 base, 50 G curse surcharge only on cursed sword base, total 215 G with fee\");\n\n  // Cursed item surcharge (50%)\n  it.todo(\"should quote a cursed sword with material steel, enchantment 3 for new customer (0 years, first insurance): 165 G\");\n\n  // High enchantment surcharge (≥5, 30%