n  const componentTypes = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n  const typeCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  let basePremium = 0;\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    basePremium += BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n    if (componentTypes.has(item.type)) {\n      typeCounts[item.type] = (typeCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Block discount: each block of 3 alike components costs 60 G instead of 3×25=75 G\n  const BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\n  const BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\n  let blockDiscount = 0;\n  for (const ct of componentTypes) {\n    const count = typeCounts[ct] ?? 0;\n    const blocks = Math.floor(count / BLOCK_SIZE);\n    const basePriceForBlock = BLOCK_SIZE * (BASE_PREMIUM[ct] ?? 0);\n    blockDiscount += blocks * (basePriceForBlock - BLOCK_PRICE);\n  }\n\n  return basePremium - blockDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE;\n}\n\n/**\n * Process a claim against an existing policy.\n * Returns { payout: number, remainingCap: number }.\n */\nexport function processClaim(\n  policy: { items: Record<string, unknown>[]; insuranceSum: number },\n  damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[]\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } {\n  throw new Error(\"Not implemented\");\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950142577},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 5: Calculate New APP Mass\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n\n```\nexport function quote(\n  items: Item[],\n  _customerContext: { yearsWithMHPCO: number; contractsSoFar: number }\n): number {\n  const componentTypes = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n  const typeCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  let basePremium = 0;\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    basePremium += BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n    if (componentTypes.has(item.type)) {\n      typeCounts[item.type] = (typeCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    }\n  }\n\n  const BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\n  const BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\n  let blockDiscount = 0;\n  for (const ct of componentTypes) {\n    const count = typeCounts[ct] ?? 0;\n    const blocks = Math.floor(count / BLOCK_SIZE);\n    const basePriceForBlock = BLOCK_SIZE * (BASE_PREMIUM[ct] ?? 0);\n    blockDiscount += blocks * (basePriceForBlock - BLOCK_PRICE);\n  }\n\n  return basePremium - blockDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE;\n}\n```\n\n**Component Count**:\n\n| Category | Items | Count | Mass |\n|----------|-------|-------|------|\n| **Constants** | `\"rune\"`, `\"moonstone\"`, `0` (in `{}`), `0` (in `let basePremium`), `0` (×2 in `??` inside for), `0` (×2 in second for `??`), `1` (in `+ 1`), `3` (BLOCK_SIZE), `60` (BLOCK_PRICE), `0` (seed `??` inside second for) | 12 | 12 |\n| **Bindings** | `items`, `_customerContext`, `componentTypes`, `typeCounts`, `basePremium`, `item`, `BLOCK_SIZE`, `BLOCK_PRICE`, `blockDiscount`, `ct`, `count`, `blocks`, `basePriceForBlock` | 13 | 13 |\n| **Invocations** | `new Set(...)`, `componentTypes.has(...)`, `Math.floor(...)`, `BASE_PREMIUM[item.type]` (index), `BASE_PREMIUM[ct]` (index), `typeCounts[item.type]` (read ×1), `??` (×4), `+=` (addition part ×2), `+`, `-`, `*`, iteration of Set via for-of | ~12 | 24 |\n| **Conditionals** | `if (componentTypes.has(item.type))` | 1 | 4 |\n| **Loops** | `for (const item of items)`, `for (const ct of componentTypes)` | 2 | 10 |\n| **Assignments** | `basePremium += ...`, `typeCounts[...] = ...`, `blockDiscount += ...` | 3 | 18 |\n\n**Total New Mass**: 12 + 13 + 24 + 4 + 10 + 18 = **81**\n\n## Mass Comparison\n\n| Metric | Before | After | Delta |\n|--------|--------|-------|-------|\n| Constants | 13 | 12 | -1 |\n| Bindings | 13 | 13 | 0 |\n| Invocations | 30 | 24 | -6 |\n| Conditionals | 0 | 4 | +4 |\n| Loops | 15 | 10 | -5 |\n| Assignments | 12 | 18 | +6 |\n| **Total** | **83** | **81** | **-2** |\n\nNet mass reduced by 2. The biggest win is collapsing two loops (reduce + for-of) into a single pass, dropping from 3 loops to 2 (mass: 15→10).\n\n## Step 6: Document Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n\n- **Naming**: Renamed `base` → `basePremium` (better reveals intent that it's the total premium sum before discounts)\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Extracted `BLOCK_SIZE` and `BLOCK_PRICE` constants with explanatory names; computed `basePriceForBlock` from `BASE_PREMIUM[ct]` rather than hardcoding `75`, making the block discount formula self-documenting (`blockPriceForBlock - BLOCK_PRICE` instead of `75 - 60`)\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: Merged two separate passes over `items` (type counting + premium summing) into a single `for` loop, eliminating duplicate iteration\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: Derived `basePriceForBlock` from `BASE_PREMIUM[ct]` instead of hardcoding `75`, removing the knowledge duplication between `BASE_PREMIUM[\"rune\"] = 25` and the constant `75` (which was really `3 × 25`)\n- **Mass**: Reduced from 83 to 81 (delta -2)\n- **Rule 4 trade-off**: Added 1 conditional (`if componentTypes.has`) and 1 extra assignment, but the clarity gain and loop reduction justifies the small net cost\n\n**Benefits**:\n1. Single-pass algorithm — no redundant iteration\n2. Block discount formula now derived from `BASE_PREMIUM` — if rune/moonstone premiums ever changed, the block discount would automatically adjust\n3. Constants `BLOCK_SIZE` and `BLOCK_PRICE` self-document the business rules\n4. `basePremium` name clearly reveals intent\n\n---\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring**: Merged two-pass iteration into single pass; renamed `base` → `basePremium`; extracted named constants for block discount logic; derived block base price from `BASE_PREMIUM` instead of hardcoding `75`.\n\n**Mass Change**: 83 → 81 (-2)\n\n**Tests**: All 8 passing ✓"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1159,"output":1305,"cacheRead":12032,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14496,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784950142578,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-178cac21-d8ea-4bab-9639-22e548589ddd","responseModel":"deepseek/dee