 \"every group of\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1c7da1803b7b46cb85e744b7","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-24-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":701,"output":276,"cacheRead":41472,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":42449,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950155654,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-e803d095-87b9-4d22-ab5c-0730ec7841d1","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_1c7da1803b7b46cb85e744b7","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/**\n * MHPCO Claim Office - quote and claim processing logic.\n */\n\n/** Processing fee applied to every quote (in G). */\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\n/** Base premium amounts per item type (in G). */\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\n/** An insurable item. */\ntype Item = {\n  type: string;\n  material: string;\n  enchantment: number;\n  cursed: boolean;\n};\n\n/**\n * Quote: compute the premium for a list of items for a given customer state.\n * Returns the total premium in G (integer).\n */\nexport function quote(\n  items: Item[],\n  _customerContext: { yearsWithMHPCO: number; contractsSoFar: number }\n): number {\n  // Single pass: sum base premiums and count component types for block discount\n  const componentTypes = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n  const typeCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  let basePremium = 0;\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    basePremium += BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n    if (componentTypes.has(item.type)) {\n      typeCounts[item.type] = (typeCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Block discount: each block of 3 alike components costs 60 G instead of 3×25=75 G\n  const BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\n  const BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\n  let blockDiscount = 0;\n  for (const ct of componentTypes) {\n    const count = typeCounts[ct] ?? 0;\n    const blocks = Math.floor(count / BLOCK_SIZE);\n    const basePriceForBlock = BLOCK_SIZE * (BASE_PREMIUM[ct] ?? 0);\n    blockDiscount += blocks * (basePriceForBlock - BLOCK_PRICE);\n  }\n\n  return basePremium - blockDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE;\n}\n\n/**\n * Process a claim against an existing policy.\n * Returns { payout: number, remainingCap: number }.\n */\nexport function processClaim(\n  policy: { items: Record<string, unknown>[]; insuranceSum: number },\n  damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[]\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } {\n  throw new Error(\"Not implemented\");\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950157649},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Wait... The spec says: \"A building block of 3 alike components is offered at a special base premium of 60 G.\" The examples: \"3 runes → 60 G (block applies)\" and \"4 runes → 100 G base premium (no block — block requires exactly 3)\". But 4 runes = 100 G, which is 4×25 = 100. That means blocks only apply to sets of exactly 3, not every 3.\n\nBut then: \"7 runes → 175 G base premium.\" 7×25 = 175. That's consistent — no block because 7 isn't 3. But... 6 runes would be 2 blocks: 2×60 = 120. And \"3 runes + 3 moonstones → 120 G base premium (two separate blocks)\". So 6 = 2×(3) = 2 blocks.\n\nSo the rule is: a block is exactly 3 of the same type. Multiple blocks are allowed. 4 runes: no block because 4 is not divisible by 3 exactly. 7 runes: no block. Only exact multiples of 3 count.\n\nThe current code: `blocks = Math.floor(count / 3)` → 4/3 = 1 block. But the spec expects 0 blocks for 4 (no blocks for non-exact-3 sets). Wait re-reading: \"4 runes → 100 G base premium (no block — block requires exactly 3)\".\n\nSo the spec means: the block concept requires exactly 3. 4 runes = no block at all. Not \"one block of 3 + one extra rune\". It seems they define a \"building block\" as exactly 3, and a set of 4 doesn't \"contain\" a block — you only get the block price when you have exactly a multiple of 3.\n\nSo: block discount ONLY when count is exactly divisible by 3, and then all items are at block rate (60 per 3).\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_212e556249b841a6b2527213","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"    const count = typeCounts[ct] ?? 0;\n    if (count % BLOCK_SIZE === 0 && count > 0) {\n      const blocks = count / BLOCK_SIZE;\n      const basePriceForBlock = BLOCK_SIZE * (BASE_PREMIUM[ct] ?? 0);\n      blockDiscount += blocks * (basePriceForBlock - BLOCK_PRICE);\n    }","oldText":"    const count = typeCounts[ct] ?? 0;\n    const blocks = Math.floor(count / BLOCK_SIZE);\n    const basePriceForBlock = BLOCK_SIZE * (BASE_PREMIUM[ct] ?? 0);\n    blockDiscount += blocks * (basePriceForBlock - BLOCK_PRICE);"}],"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-24-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":764,"output":713,"cacheRead":42240,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":43717,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950157653,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-5169b9f7-39d1-498d-9c4f-e081b695721d","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_212e556249b841a6b2527213","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-24-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"    ...\n 48   const BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\n 49   let blockDiscount = 0;\n 50   for (const ct of componentTypes) {\n 51     const cou