ests 3ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950268739},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 13 tests still green. Let me verify the final state of the file:\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_beeb6005a35f42559b40d40d","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":255,"output":63,"cacheRead":15360,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":15678,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950268740,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-62cde16a-13af-4d7d-9c58-a516d2dfff75","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_beeb6005a35f42559b40d40d","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/**\n * MHPCO Claim Office - quote and claim processing logic.\n */\n\n/** Processing fee applied to every quote (in G). */\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\n/** Base premium amounts per item type (in G). */\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\n/** Item types eligible for block discounts (components). */\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\n/** An insurable item. */\ntype Item = {\n  type: string;\n  material: string;\n  enchantment: number;\n  cursed: boolean;\n};\n\n/**\n * Quote: compute the premium for a list of items for a given customer state.\n * Returns the total premium in G (integer).\n */\nexport function quote(\n  items: Item[],\n  _customerContext: { yearsWithMHPCO: number; contractsSoFar: number }\n): number {\n  // Single pass: sum base premiums, count component types, and track item-specific surcharges\n  const typeCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  let basePremium = 0;\n  let itemSurcharges = 0;\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    const itemBase = BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n    basePremium += itemBase;\n    // Cursed: 50% surcharge on item's base premium\n    if (item.cursed) {\n      itemSurcharges += itemBase * 0.5;\n    }\n    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      typeCounts[item.type] = (typeCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Block discount: each block of 3 alike components costs 60 G instead of 3×25=75 G\n  let blockDiscount = 0;\n  for (const ct of COMPONENT_TYPES) {\n    const count = typeCounts[ct] ?? 0;\n    if (count % 3 === 0) {\n      blockDiscount += count * 5;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return basePremium + itemSurcharges - blockDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE;\n}\n\n/**\n * Process a claim against an existing policy.\n * Returns { payout: number, remainingCap: number }.\n */\nexport function processClaim(\n  policy: { items: Record<string, unknown>[]; insuranceSum: number },\n  damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[]\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } {\n  throw new Error(\"Not implemented\");\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950269612},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\n\n## Step 5: Calculate New APP Mass\n\n```\n// Refactored code:\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n// Constants: 1. Bindings: 1.  Mass: 2\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100, amulet: 60, staff: 80, potion: 40, rune: 25, moonstone: 25,\n};\n// Constants: 6. Bindings: 1.  Mass: 7\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n// Constants: 2. Bindings: 1. Invocations: 1 (new Set).  Mass: 2 + 1 + 2 = 5\n\nexport function quote(items, _customerContext) {\n// Bindings: 2.  Mass: 2\n\n  const typeCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  // Bindings: 1.  Mass: 1\n\n  let basePremium = 0;\n  // Constants: 1. Bindings: 1.  Mass: 2\n\n  let itemSurcharges = 0;\n  // Constants: 1. Bindings: 1.  Mass: 2\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n  // Loops: 1. Bindings: 1.  Mass: 6\n\n    const itemBase = BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n    // Constants: 1. Bindings: 1. Invocations: 2 ([], ??).  Mass: 6\n\n    basePremium += itemBase;\n    // Assignments: 1. Invocations: 1 (+=).  Mass: 8\n\n    if (item.cursed) {\n    // Conditionals: 1.  Mass: 4\n\n      itemSurcharges += itemBase * 0.5;\n      // Constants: 1. Assignments: 1. Invocations: 2 (*, +=).  Mass: 9\n    }\n\n    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n    // Conditionals: 1. Invocations: 1 (.has).  Mass: 6\n\n      typeCounts[item.type] = (typeCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n      // Constants: 2. Assignments: 1. Invocations: 4 ([], [], ??, +).  Mass: 12\n    }\n  }\n\n  let blockDiscount = 0;\n  // Constants: 1. Bindings: 1.  Mass: 2\n\n  for (const ct of COMPONENT_TYPES) {\n  // Loops: 1. Bindings: 1.  Mass: 6\n\n    const count = typeCounts[ct] ?? 0;\n    // Constants: 1. Bindings: 1. Invocations: 2 ([], ??).  Mass: 6\n\n    if (count % 3 === 0) {\n    // Conditionals: 1. Invocations: 1 (%). Constants: 1.  Mass: 7\n\n      blockDiscount += count * 5;\n      // Constants: 1. Assignments: 1. Invocations: 2 (*, +=).  Mass: 9\n    }\n  }\n\n  return basePremium + itemSurcharges - blockDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  // Invocations: 3 (+, -, +).  Mass: 6 (no bindings - these are references, counted as invocations)\n}\n```\n\n**Post-refactor totals (function body only, plus module-level shared with function)**:\n\nActually, let me compute just the function body for a fair before/after comparison, since module-level constants existed before too.\n\n**Before (function `quote` body only)**:\n- Constants: 2 (\"rune\", \"moonstone\" in Set) + 1 (0 in basePremium) + 1 (0 in itemSurcharges) + 1 (0 in ?? itemBase) + 1 (0.5) + 2 (0, 1 in typeCounts) + 1 (0 in blockDiscount) + 2 (0, 3 in count check) + 1 (0 in count > 0) + 1 (5 in blockDiscount) = **13**\n- Bindings: 1 (componentTypes) + 1 (typeCounts) + 1 (basePremium) + 1 (itemSurcharges) + 1 (item loop) + 1 (itemBase) + 1 (blockDiscount) + 1 (ct loop) + 1 (count) + 2 (items, _customerContext params) = **11**\n- Invocations: 1 (new Set) + 