e surcharge (10%)\n\nFirst insurance: 10% on policy base premium. The spec says: \"A first insurance carries a 10 % initial assessment surcharge\" and from the clarifying question: \"The first insurance surcharge still applies to the new sword, even though the customer is on a follow-up contract — each item in a quote is treated as a first insurance, regardless of customer history.\"\n\nSo first insurance applies per-item, not per-policy. Every item in a quote is a \"first insurance\" forever. That means all items get 10% added.\n\nActually, wait. The integration example: \"customer: 0 years with MHPCO, no previous contract; item: a cursed sword (steel, enchantment 3); premium: 165 G; (100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance = 160 + 5 fee = 165)\". The 10 first insurance is 10% of 100 = 10. And it's per each quote, not per item. Let me re-read the clarifying question:\n\nFrom the spec: \"- A first insurance carries a 10 % initial assessment surcharge.\" \nClarifying: \"Wait — does 'first insurance' mean the customer's first ever contract, or the first time we see this particular item? A long-standing customer with a brand-new sword: does the first insurance surcharge still apply?\"\n\nResolution: The first insurance surcharge ALWAYS applies. \"Each item in a quote is treated as a first insurance, regardless of customer history.\"\n\nSo first insurance surcharge = 10% of each item's base premium? Or 10% of total policy base premium? Let me check the integration example:\n\n\"100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance = 160 + 5 fee = 165\"\n10 = 10% of 100 (sword base). So it's 10% of each item's base. Simple: always apply.\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_a772acd175084d61adfd8703","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-24-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":668,"output":632,"cacheRead":53248,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":54548,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950284930,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-168d9555-f136-456f-9a89-013aa4951c00","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_a772acd175084d61adfd8703","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/**\n * MHPCO Claim Office - quote and claim processing logic.\n */\n\n/** Processing fee applied to every quote (in G). */\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\n/** Base premium amounts per item type (in G). */\nconst BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\n/** Item types eligible for block discounts (components). */\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\n/** An insurable item. */\ntype Item = {\n  type: string;\n  material: string;\n  enchantment: number;\n  cursed: boolean;\n};\n\n/**\n * Quote: compute the premium for a list of items for a given customer state.\n * Returns the total premium in G (integer).\n */\nexport function quote(\n  items: Item[],\n  _customerContext: { yearsWithMHPCO: number; contractsSoFar: number }\n): number {\n  // Single pass: sum base premiums, count component types, and track item-specific surcharges\n  const typeCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  let basePremium = 0;\n  let itemSurcharges = 0;\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    const itemBase = BASE_PREMIUM[item.type] ?? 0;\n    basePremium += itemBase;\n    // Cursed: 50% surcharge on item's base premium\n    if (item.cursed) {\n      itemSurcharges += itemBase * 0.5;\n    }\n    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      typeCounts[item.type] = (typeCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Block discount: each block of 3 alike components costs 60 G instead of 3×25=75 G\n  let blockDiscount = 0;\n  for (const ct of COMPONENT_TYPES) {\n    const count = typeCounts[ct] ?? 0;\n    if (count % 3 === 0) {\n      blockDiscount += count * 5;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return basePremium + itemSurcharges - blockDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE;\n}\n\n/**\n * Process a claim against an existing policy.\n * Returns { payout: number, remainingCap: number }.\n */\nexport function processClaim(\n  policy: { items: Record<string, unknown>[]; insuranceSum: number },\n  damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[]\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } {\n  throw new Error(\"Not implemented\");\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950289003},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The first insurance surcharge is 10% on the total base premium (not per-item). For 100 base + 50 cursed = 150, + 10 first insurance = 160, + 5 fee = 165. The first insurance is 10% of base premium = 10.\n\nBut wait — is it on the base premium or on the base + cursed? The spec example breaks down as \"100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance.\" The 10 first insurance is definitely 10% of base (100 × 0.1). So first insurance = 10% of total base premium (sum of all item bases, before modifiers). Let me add it.\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_da43ff25d5b44f66b4e2d6b2","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"  // Block discount: each block of 3 alike components costs 60 G instead of 3×25=75 G\n  let blockDiscount = 0;\n  for (const ct of COMPONENT_TYPES) {\n    const count = typeCounts[ct] ?? 0;\n    if (count % 3 === 0) {\n      blockDiscount += count * 5;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // First insurance surcharge: 10% on base premium (applies to every quote)\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = basePremium * 0.1;\n\n  return basePremium + itemSurcharges + firstInsuranceSurcharge - blockDiscount + PROCESSING_FEE;","oldText":"  // Block discount: each block of 3 alike components costs 60 G instead of 3×25=75 G\n  let blockDiscount = 0;\n  for (const ct of COMPONENT_TYPES) {\n    const count = typeCounts[ct] ?? 0;\n    i