,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good. Now let me calculate the new APP mass.\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: Refactored APP Mass\n\nThe new constants are module-level, not in the function, so the function body mass changes subtly. Let me recount the function body only (module-level constants are shared infrastructure):\n\n**In `quote` function body:**\n- **Constants**: `0` (initial: totalBasePremium=0, itemSurcharges=0, blockSavings=0), `?? 0` (x3), `1` (increment) = 7 → **7**\n- **Bindings**: `typeCounts`, `totalBasePremium`, `itemSurcharges`, `itemBase`, `blockSavings`, `ct`, `count`, `basePremium`, `firstInsuranceSurcharge`, `rawPremium` = 10 → **10**\n- **Invocations**: `COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)`, `Math.ceil(rawPremium)` = 2 → **4**\n- **Conditionals**: `item.cursed`, `item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD`, `COMPONENT_TYPES.has(...)`, `count % COMPONENTS_PER_BLOCK === 0` = 4 → **16**\n- **Loops**: `for (const item of items)`, `for (const ct of COMPONENT_TYPES)` = 2 → **10**\n- **Assignments**: `totalBasePremium +=`, `itemSurcharges +=` (x2), `typeCounts[...] =`, `blockSavings +=` = 5 → **30**\n\n**Function body total: 7 + 10 + 4 + 16 + 10 + 30 = 77** (down from 83)\n\nThe function body mass dropped because magic number literals (`5`, `0.5`, `0.3`, `0.1`, `3`, `5`) moved to module-level named constants. Module constants are shared infrastructure, not duplicated per call.\n\n**Module-level constants (counted once)**: `5`, `0.5`, `0.3`, `5`, `0.1`, `100`, `60`, `80`, `40`, `25`, `25`, `\"rune\"`, `\"moonstone\"`, `3`, `5` = 15 → **15** (same count, but now all named)\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Document Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Extracted 6 magic numbers as named module-level constants:\n  - `CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE` (0.5) — self-documents what the 50% is for\n  - `HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE` (0.3) — self-documents the 30% surcharge\n  - `HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD` (5) — clarifies what \"≥5\" gates\n  - `FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE` (0.1) — names the 10% rate\n  - `COMPONENTS_PER_BLOCK` (3) — clarifies the block-size constant\n  - `BLOCK_SAVING_PER_ITEM` (5) — names the per-item saving amount\n\n- **Mass**: Function body reduced from 83 → 77 (delta -6). The removed magic numbers became named module constants, reducing function-local constant count while improving clarity.\n\n**Benefits**:\n1. Magic numbers now have explicit domain names — someone reading the code immediately knows what `CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE` means without needing the comment\n2. Single point of change: if the business rules change (e.g., cursed surcharge goes from 50% to 60%), only one constant needs updating\n3. Lower function body mass (77 vs 83) while maintaining identical behavior\n\n**Tests**: All 15 passing, no regressions.\n\n---\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring**: Extracted 6 magic numbers as named module-level constants (Rule 2: Reveals Intent)\n**Mass Change**: 83 → 77 in function body (delta -6)\n**Tests**: All 15 passing ✅"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-24-15_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 15\nRecent Green phase: Added high-enchantment surcharge (≥5, 30%) alongside the cursed surcharge (50%) in the item loop. Both item-specific modifiers are now computed in the same for loop.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 15\nRecent Green phase: Added high-enchantment surcharge (≥5, 30%) alongside the cursed surcharge (50%) in the item loop. Both item-specific modifiers are now computed in the same for loop.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784950366051},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'll start by reading the current implementation and test files to understand the codebase before refactoring"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_6f26a91161434d7f95ee206e","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_a371eba378af471a8be655df","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":233,"output":103,"cacheRead":6144,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6480,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950366071,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-8a5d0daf-b44b-4779-b646-09a8dfe69c7e","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6f26a91161434d7f95ee206e","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/**\n * MHPCO Claim Office - quote and claim processing logic.\n */\n\n/** Processing fee applied to every quote (in G). */\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\n/** Base premium amounts per item type (in G). Raw per-item price. */\nconst ITEM_BASE_PRICE: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\n/** Item types eligible for block discounts (components). */\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\n/** An insurable item. */\ntype Item = {\n  type: string;\n  material: string;\n  enchantment: number;\n  cursed: boolean;\n};\n\n/**\n * Quote: compute the premium for a list of items for a given customer state.\n * Returns the total premium in G (integer).\n */\nexport function quote(\n  items: Item[],\n  _customerContext: { yearsWithMHPCO: number; contractsSoFar: number }\n): number {\n  const typeCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  let totalBasePremium = 0;\n  let itemSurcharges = 0;\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    const itemBase = ITEM_BASE_PRICE[item.type] ?? 0;\n    totalBasePremium += itemBase;\n    // Cursed: 50% surcharge on item's base premium\n    if (item.cursed) {\n      itemSurcharges += itemBase * 0.5;\n    }\n    // High enchantment (≥5): 30% surcharge on item's base premium\n    if (item.enchantment >= 5) {\n      itemSurcharges += itemBase * 0.3;\n    }\n    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      typeCounts[item.type] = (typeCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Block savings: each block of 3 alike components costs 60 instead of 3×25=75\n  let blockSavings = 0;\n  for (const ct of COMPONENT_TYPES) {\n    const count = typeCounts[ct] ?? 0;\n    if (count % 3 === 0) {\n      blockSavings += count * 5;\n    }\n  }\n  const basePremium = totalBasePremium - blockSavings;\n\n  // First insurance surcharge: 10% on base premium (applies to every quote)\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = basePremium * 0.1;\n\n  const rawPremium = basePremium + itemSurcharges + firstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE;\n  // Round up (MHPCO's favor) to nearest whole G\n  return Math.ceil(rawPremium);\n}\n\n/**\n * Process a claim against an existing policy.\n * Returns { payout: number, remainingCap: number }.\n */\nexport function processClaim(\n  policy: { items: Record<string, unknown>[]; insuranceSum: number },\n  damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[]\n): { payout: number; remainingCap: number } {\n  throw new Error(\"Not implemented\");\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950368195},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_a371eba378af471a8be655df","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { quote, processClaim } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office\", () => {\n  // === QUOTE TESTS ===\n\n  // Empty item list\n  it(\"should quote 5 G for empty item list (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(5);\n  });\n\n  // Single items - base premiums (with first insurance 10%)\n  it(\"should quote 115 G for a plain sword (100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 71 G for a plain amulet (60 base + 6 first insurance + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 93 G for a plain staff (80 base + 8 first insurance + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"staff\", material: \"wood\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(93);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 49 G for a plain potion (40 base + 4 first insurance + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"potion\", material: \"glass\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(49);\n  });\n\n  // Components (with first insurance 10% on base)\n  it(\"should quote 33 G for a single rune (25 base + 2.5 first insurance + 5 fee, rounded up)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(33);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 60 G for 2 runes (50 base + 5 first insurance + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }, { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 71 G for 3 runes (60 block base + 6 first insurance + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }, { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }, { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 115 G for 4 runes (100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([\n      { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n    ], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 198 G for 7 runes (175 base + 17.5 first insurance + 5 fee, rounded up = 197.5 → 198)\", () => {\n    const runes = Array(7).fill(null).map(() => ({ type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }));\n    expect(quote(runes, { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(198);\n  });\n\n  // \"Alike\" components - clarifying question test\n  it(\"should quote 88 G for 2 runes + 1 moonstone (75 base + 7.5 first insurance + 5 fee, rounded up)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([\n      { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      { type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n      { type: \"moonstone\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n    ], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(88);\n  });\n  it(\"should quote 137 G for 3 runes + 3 moonstones (120 block base + 12 first insurance + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    const runes = Array(3).fill(null).map(() => ({ type: \"rune\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }));\n    const moonstones = Array(3).fill(null).map(() => ({ type: \"moonstone\", material: \"stone\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false }));\n    expect(quote([...runes, ...moonstones], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(137);\n  });\n\n  // Modifier scope on multi-item policies\n  it(\"should quote cursed sword (100 base) + plain amulet (60 base) = 160 base, 50 curse + 16 first insurance + 5 fee = 231 G\", () => {\n    expect(quote([\n      { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 0, cursed: true },\n      { type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 0, cursed: false },\n    ], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(231);\n  });\n\n  // Cursed item surcharge (50%)\n  // Newcomer with a cursed sword\n  it(\"should quote 165 G for newcomer (0 years, first contract) with cursed sword (steel, enchantment 3)\", () => {\n    expect(quote([\n      { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true },\n    ], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(165);\n  });\n\n  // High enchantment surcharge (≥5, 30%)\n  it(\"should quote a highly enchanted (level 5) non-cursed sword: 100 base + 30 enchantment + 10 first insurance + 5 fee = 145 G\", () => {\n    expect(quote([{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }], { yearsWithMHPCO: 0, contractsSoFar: 0 })).toBe(145);\n  });\n\n  // Thresholds\n  it.todo(\"should apply loyalty discount at exactly 2 years with MHPCO\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply high-enchantment surcharge at exactly enchantment 5; also apply curse if cursed\");\n  it.todo(\"should NOT apply high-enchantment surcharge at enchantment 4\");\n  \n  // Loyalty discount (≥2 years, 20%)\n  it.todo(\"should quote a sword with loyalty discount (≥2 years): 100 base - 20 loyalty = 85 G with fee\");\n\n  // First insurance surcharge (10%)\n  it.todo(\"should quote a sword for first insurance (no previous contracts): 100 base + 10 first insurance = 115 G with fee\");\n\n  // Follow-up contract discount (15% on each after first)\n  it.todo(\"should quote a sword for follow-up (not first) contract: 100 base - 15 follow-up = 90 G with fee\");\n\n  // Multiple items of same type\n  it.todo(\"should quote two swords: insurance sum 2000 G, base premium 200 G + fee\");\n\n  // Long-standing customer second contract integration example\n  it.todo(\"should quote 160 G for long-standing customer (3 years), second contract, cursed sword (steel, enchantment 7)\");\n\n  // Newcomer with cursed sword integration example\n  it.todo(\"should quote 165 G for newcomer (0 years, first contract) with cursed sword (steel, enchantment 3)\");\n\n  // Rounding in MHPCO's favor\n  it.todo(\"should round premium 197.5 G up to 198 G\");\n\n  // Unknown item type\n  it.todo(\"should reject quote with unknown item type (broomstick)\");\n\n  // Policy tracking for multi-step scenarios\n  it.todo(\"should support quoting two policies and referencing them correctly\");\n\n  // ===== CLAIM TESTS =====\n\n  // Basic deductible\n  it.todo(\"should process claim for regular steel sword (enchantment 3), damage 500 G → payout 400 G\");\n\n  // Standard reimbursement for rune (no special clause)\n  it.todo(\"should process claim for rune damage 200 G → payout 100 G\");\n\n  // Deductible per damage event (per damaged item)\n  it.todo(\"should process claim for dragon attack damaging sword (500) and amulet (300): payout 600 G\");\n\n  // Enchantment level ≥ 8: 50% reimbursement\n  it.todo(\"should process claim for enchantment 8 sword (no dragon), damage 1000 G → payout 400 G (500 half - 100 ded)\");\n\n  // Dragon material: full reimbursement\n  it.todo(\"should process claim for dragon-material sword (enchantment 5), damage 800 G → payout 700 G\");\n\n  // Both clauses: enchantment 9, dragon material\n  it.todo(\"should process claim for dragon-material sword enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → payout 400 G (50% wins, then deductible)\");\n\n  // Enchantment 8 exactly, dragon material\n  it.todo(\"should process claim for dragon-material sword enchantment 8, damage 1000 G → payout 400 G\");\n\n  // Steel enchantment 9 – only high enchantment clause applies\n  it.todo(\"should process claim for steel sword enchantment 9, damage 1000